# Coding Rules

## Standards
- keep modules small and focused
- define interfaces before deep implementation
- use explicit types
- add comments only where they clarify assumptions or tricky behavior
- log important migration and reconciliation events
- do not silently swallow failures

## Implementation Preferences
- connectors should wrap external API behavior cleanly
- transformers should be deterministic and testable
- repositories should be simple and auditable
- migration services should be resumable where possible
- reconciliation should be batch-oriented and easy to inspect

## Testing Focus
Prioritize tests for:
- status mapping
- comment visibility mapping
- chronology preservation
- attachment workflow
- idempotent reruns
- reconciliation mismatch detection
